course: dictionary
lesson: 81
title: Active: moving, taking part, working
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Children should be active for at least an hour a day.» Here active means moving around and doing things a lot, like running, playing and sport. Your heart and muscles need this to stay strong.
explain: Active has other meanings too. «She is an active member of the club» means she takes part and helps out. An active volcano is one that can still erupt. Look at the words around active to find which meaning fits.
explain: In grammar, an active sentence is one where the subject does the action: «The dog chased the ball.» The dog does the chasing. Quick check: ask who is doing the action. If the answer is the subject, the sentence is active.
fact: Active is an adjective: active, more active, most active.
fact: «Active» means moving around and doing things a lot.
fact: «Active» also means working or taking part in something, like an active member of a club.
fact: An active volcano is one that can still erupt.
fact: «Mice are mostly active at night» means they are awake and moving about then.
exercise: «Children should be active for at least an hour a day.» What does active mean here? | Asleep in bed | Sitting still and quiet | Angry with other people | *Moving around and doing things a lot
exercise: «Mice are mostly active at night.» What does active mean here? | Full of colour | *Awake and moving about | Busy with homework | Hidden under the floor
exercise: Which sentence is an active sentence? | *The dog chased the ball. | The ball is round. | The ball was chased by the dog. | The ball was round and red.
test: «An active volcano is one that can still erupt.» In this sentence, active means | Sleeping for ever | *Able to erupt | Covered in snow | Small and quiet
test: Which phrase means joining in with something? | Go to sleep | Lose the game | *Take an active part | Sit very still
exam: «Dried tardigrades survive great cold, but active tardigrades are quite fragile.» Here active means | Very old | *Alive and moving, not dried up | Frozen solid | Small and round
